# Motif fileview smoke for the language dialog render/input path.
#
# scripts/run-ui-replay.py's `button N click` translates internally to
# press + delay + release for the LIBX11_COMPAT_REPLAY engine.
delay 2500
wait-window "fileview|File" 3000
# Let Motif's initial reflow drain before the first snapshot. fileview
# starts a language dialog whose pixmap/Expose churn can stretch past
# the prior fixed 500 ms ceiling, which is what surfaced the snapshot
# timeout in run-to-run nondeterminism.
wait-converge 200 2 50 200 15000
screenshot initial
assert-image initial common-visible.json
# target-motion is relative to the current replay target window, which matches
# the in-process snapshot coordinate space. (119, 480) lands on the Done button
# in fileview's language-selection dialog. The click is delivered as input
# coverage: it routes through convertEvent and fires fileview's DoneCallback,
# which is the dialog input path this smoke exercises.
#
# Nothing after the click is asserted, on purpose. fileview's own main() responds
# to Done by closing its sole X display and opening a fresh one, then rebuilding
# its whole UI on the new display. The in-process model does a full SDL_Quit and
# reinitialize on last-display XCloseDisplay and hands the second XOpenDisplay the
# same singleton globals, so the Xt/Motif resource ids (GCs, fonts) cached against
# the first display are stranded on the second. libx11-compat no longer crashes on
# the stranded ids it touches (a NULL font face reaching SDL_ttf, a freed GC in
# XGetGCValues, and the default error handler terminating on the resulting BadFont
# are all fixed), but rebuilding the entire UI across a sole-display close/reopen
# is a deeper limitation tracked separately, so this smoke stops at the click.
target-motion 119 480
button 1 click
